# One runnable app

The only user-facing build is the launch folder next to this checkout:

`<repo>\dist\CabinetNC-Cut\CabinetNC.Desktop.exe`

(`OmniCamDistDir` MSBuild property / `OMNICAM_DIST_DIR` env can redirect it per
machine — e.g. a fixed shop path — but nothing in the repo may hardcode a drive
letter.)

Desktop icon `OmniCam` and `OmniCam.cmd` start that folder.

Do not create extra copies (`dist\CabinetNC-Cut-fd*`, `*-stage4`, `*-next`, `*-old`, `*-win-x64`). After Desktop/Domain changes, `dotnet build -c Release` the Desktop project; PostBuild copies into the launch folder and prints `Updated desktop launch folder: <path>` — check that line if the app looks stale. If copy fails, the app is open — close it and rebuild. Tell the user to reopen from the desktop icon.
